/-!
# Words for the J₂ Sylow overgroup sieve

These 72 words are proposed double-coset representatives for the fixed `Seed.s`.
They are elements of the actual degree-100 carrier by construction. `Covers`
is the separate exhaustiveness obligation. The accompanying short words are
candidate elements of order five; their orders and the six exceptional
normalizer memberships require separate kernel checks.

The retained data in `source/double-cosets.json` were found by `source/discover.g`.
The conversion from the ATLAS right action to Lean's left action preserves
word order. No GAP assertion about orders, double cosets, or normalizers is
used as a proof here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, proof of Proposition 1.3.4, printed p.511
(PDF p.528 of `refs/quasithin.pdf`), and GLS3 Table 5.3g. Original ATLAS
permutations and attribution are retained in `AtlasCarriers/source/`.
-/

